.TH auto-wifi-failover 8

\" auto-man2man (used in generating subcommand lists) depends on this section
.SH NAME
.PP
auto-wifi-failover - Configure Ethernet to WiFi failover

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-wifi-failover [wired-interface wireless-interface]
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
wired-interface     The Ethernet interface to use when available
wireless-interface  The WiFi interface to use when Ethernet is down
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-wifi-failover
command configures networking to use Ethernet when available
and fail over to WiFi when Ethernet is unplugged.

If run with no arguments, the user is prompted for wired and
wireless interfaces.

The user can optionally indicate the wired and wireless interfaces
on the command line, in which case both must be provided.

On FreeBSD, this is performed using the link aggregation [lagg(4)]
driver, which requires the interfaces to use the same MAC address.
Some common WiFi devices do not support altering the MAC address, so
.B auto-wifi-failover
attempts to set the wired device MAC to match the WiFi device.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-wifi-failover
auto-wifi-failover re0 ath0
.ad
.fi

.SH FILES
.nf
.na
/etc/rc.conf
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-admin(8), auto-network-config(8), auto-network-manager(8),
auto-network-restart(8), ifconfig(8)

